  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "17. Monsters And Vehicles",
    "ruleNumber": "17.03",
    "summary": "In your Shooting phase, ranged fire can target an enemy MONSTER or VEHICLE even if it is Engaged. Leave [BLAST] out of those attacks. Reduce the attack's Hit roll by 1, with one exception. A weapon marked [CLOSE-QUARTERS] avoids the reduction when the firer's unit is itself Engaged with that enemy. If the firing unit cannot shoot and is Engaged with that enemy, it needs Close-Quarters Shooting to attack it. Apply the limits of that shooting type. The example shows an unengaged INFANTRY unit firing at a VEHICLE with normal shooting at −1. The Engaged INFANTRY unit in the example can return fire at that VEHICLE using only its [CLOSE-QUARTERS] weapons. The VEHICLE uses Close-Quarters Shooting against both INFANTRY units. It excludes [BLAST] against the engaged unit, and can aim [BLAST] at other unengaged units.",
    "summarySpans": [
